      "message": "Fixed. `slugify` no longer produces repeated dashes.\n\n**The bug:** every non-alphanumeric character appended its own `-`, so `\"Hello   World!!\"` came out as `hello---world--`.\n\n**The fix** (`slug/core.py`, last line): the output is split on `-`, empty pieces are dropped, and the rest is rejoined with single dashes. Runs of separators collapse to one dash, and leading or trailing dashes are stripped.\n\n**Quick check** (I ran four inputs, not the test suite):\n- `\"Hello   World!!\"` → `hello-world`\n- `\"a -- b\"` → `a-b`\n- `\"Hello World\"` → `hello-world`\n- `\"  ABC  \"` → `abc`\n\nOne behavior change to be aware of: leading and trailing dashes are now stripped, so `\"Hello World!\"` gives `hello-world`, not `hello-world-`. I didn't run `tests/test_core.py`, so that's unverified.",
